 "transcript": [
  "Wang Lung (to the second son): \"Well, and what are you about then?\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and I will not be a day's journey from the town. The market will be a great place. We will have a great deal of money, and we will have a great house and we will have many servants.\"",
  "[says] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung expresses his approval of his son's plans.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and do what you will, my son. If I have land, I will not be without slaves, and we will have the house in the town as well as on my land.\"",
  "[action] goes into hut",
  "[action] Wang Lung goes into the hut, where Pear Blossom lives.",
  "Wang Lung: \"Tell me what you have eaten.\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung sits on his bed.",
  "[action] Wang Lung looks at Pear Blossom and finds her very thin.",
  "[action] Wang Lung goes out of his hut.",
  "[action] (to the second son) Wang Lung watches his second son with longing.",
  "[action] Wang Lung looks at his sons and feels old.",
  "[action] The sons enter the house.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"And what news have you, my son?\"",
